hadiths[36]{hadithnumber,text}:
1830,Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents
1831,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, An army will invade the Ka`ba and when the invaders reach Al-Baida'"
1832,"Once the Prophett & +, or, stood on the top of a castle amongst the castles (the high buildings) of Al-Madina and said, Dof yo see what I see? (Nof doubt) I see the places spots of Al-Fitn (trials and afflictions etc.) among you houses (and these Al-Fitn will be) as numerous as the spots where rain-drops fall"""
1833,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There will be afflictions (in the near future) during which a sitting person will be better than a standing one"
1834,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, While I was sleeping"
1835,Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents
1836,The Prophett rL .*b or- once delivered speech in front of us wherein he le nothing but mentioned (abo everything that would happen till thestablishment of the Hour. Some of stored that (speech) in ou minds and some forgot it. (Aftthat speech) used tof see events taking place (whic had been referred tof in that speech) b 52. fne Boot< ofrll-Frrz I had forgotten them (before thei occurrence). Then I would recognize such events as a mand recognizes anothmand whof has been absent and then sees and recognizes him. Al-Fitnaft (trial and affliction etc.) which will spread like the waves of the sea
1837,"Once I was sitting with 'Umat .; dt c4 and he said, Whof amongst yo remembers the statement of Allah's Messeng.+ .x dL d- about Al-Fitnah(trial and affliction etc.)"" I said"
1838,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Soon the river ""Euphrates"" will disclose the treasure (the mountain) of gold"
1839,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, There are angels coming to you in succession at night"
1840,"That he heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying in the year of the Conquest (of Mecca) while he was in Mecca, Allah and His Apostle have made the selling of wine (i.e. alcoholic drinks) unlawful."""""
1841,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""The Hour will not be established till a man from Qahtan appears, driving the people with his stick."""
1842,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah created Adam in His picture"
1843,"Abu Huraira said, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'A prayer performed in congregation is twenty-five times more superior in reward to a prayer performed by a single person. The angels of the night and the angels of the day are assembled at the time of the Fajr (Morning) prayer."" Abu Huraira added, ""If you wish, you can recite:-- 'Verily! The recitation of the Qur'an in the early dawn (Morning prayer) is ever witnessed (attended by the angels of the day and the night).' (17.78)"
1844,"Abu Huraira said, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'A prayer performed in congregation is twenty-five times more superior in reward to a prayer performed by a single person. The angels of the night and the angels of the day are assembled at the time of the Fajr (Morning) prayer."" Abu Huraira added, ""If you wish, you can recite:-- 'Verily! The recitation of the Qur'an in the early dawn (Morning prayer) is ever witnessed (attended by the angels of the day and the night).' (17.78)"
1845,Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents
1846,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, This branch from Quraish will ruin the people."" The companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) asked"
1847,"Abu Huraira said, ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said, 'A prayer performed in congregation is twenty-five times more superior in reward to a prayer performed by a single person. The angels of the night and the angels of the day are assembled at the time of the Fajr (Morning) prayer."" Abu Huraira added, ""If you wish, you can recite:-- 'Verily! The recitation of the Qur'an in the early dawn (Morning prayer) is ever witnessed (attended by the angels of the day and the night).' (17.78)"
1848,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""When Khosrau is ruined, there will be no Khosrau after him; and when Caesar is ruined, their will be no Caesar after him. By Him in Whose Hands my life is, you will spend their treasures in Allah's Cause."""
1849,"I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, While I was sleeping"
1850,Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents
1851,"Umar and a group of the companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) set out with the Prophet to Ibn Saiyad. He found him playing with some boys near the hillocks of Bani Maghala. Ibn Saiyad at that time was nearing his puberty. He did not notice (the Prophet's presence) till the Prophet (ﷺ) stroked him on the back with his hand and said, Ibn Saiyad! Do you testify that I am Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)?"" Ibn Saiyad looked at him and said"
1852,"Allah Messenger-:4' or, wont along w Ubai bin Ka'b tof the garden of dat palms where Ibn Saiydd was stayin When the Prophett p-, .*r, .rr. ente ',' lH.tASt; When the Prophett /-:.J,.l ,1 mind) fyou, he meant sarat Ad- mentioned just part of the word"
1853,"(Later on) Messenger of Allah ﷺ (once again) went along with Ubai bin Ka'b to the garden of date-palms where Ibn Saiyad was staying. When the Prophet entered the garden, he started hiding himself behind the trunks of the date-palms as he wanted to hear something from the Ibn Saiyad before the latter could see him. Ibn Saiyad was lying in his bed, covered with a velvet sheet from where his murmurs were heard. Ibn Saiyad's mother saw the Prophet ﷺ while he was hiding himself behind the trunks of the date-palms. She addressed Ibn Saiyad, ""O Saf!"" (And this was his name). Ibn Saiyad got up. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Had this woman let him to himself, he would have revealed the reality of his case."" Then the Prophet ﷺ got up amongst the people, glorifying Allah as He deserves, he mentioned Ad-Dajjal, saying, ""I warn you about him (i.e. Ad-Dajjal) and there is no prophet who did not warn his nation about him, and Noah warned his nation about him, but I tell you a statement which no prophet informed his nation of. You should understand that he is a one-eyed man and Allah is not one-eyed."""
1854,This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Anas through another chain of transmitters
1855,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, No prophet was sent but that he warned his followers against the one-eyed liar (Ad-Dajjal). Beware! He is blind in one eye"
1856,Uqba bin 'Am said tof Hudhaif Won't yo relate tof us of what yof have heard from Allih's Messenger.rr. d-r
1857,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Shall I not tell you about the Dajjal a story of which no prophet told his nation? The Dajjall is one-eyed and will bring with him what will resemble Hell and Paradise"
1858,"One day Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) narrated to us a long narration about Ad-Dajjal and among the things he narrated to us, was: Ad-Dajjal will come"
1859,"c +t i Al-Mughira bin Nobody asked the SZ. fne nook ofrl&firz Prophett p +, ordl- as many questions I asked regarding Ad-Dajjdl. The Prophett /-r.rb ur ,r. said tof me, Wh worries yo about him."" I sai ""Because the people say that he w have a mountain of bread and a riv watwith him (i.e. he will hav abundance of food and water)."" The Prophett d- . said"
1860,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""There will be no town which Ad-Dajjal will not enter except Mecca and Medina, and there will be no entrance (road) (of both Mecca and Medina) but the angels will be standing in rows guarding it against him, and then Medina will shake with its inhabitants thrice (i.e. three earthquakes will take place) and Allah will expel all the non-believers and the hypocrites from it."""
1861,"heard Allah's Messengpu rrb.- saying: (It will be) from among t most wicked people whof will be livin at the time when the Hou will SZ. fne noof oterz established"""
1862,Ibn `Umar reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:The pious dreams are the seventieth part of Prophecy
1863,"Allah's Messengd-r..b.l u- said, I (have been sent) and the Hou (is at hand) as these twof (fingers)."" The interval between the twof blowings of the trumpet (on the Day of Resurrection). . Nanated Al-'Amash .of ru ! Ab Huraira t* dt s-ts said"
1864,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""If Allah makes us victorious, our encamping place will be Al-Khaif, the place where the infidels took an oath to be loyal to Heathenism (by boycotting Banu Hashim, the Prophet's folk)."
1865,"Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, When carried to his grave"
